  "notes": "{自制|じせい} means controlling oneself, particularly one's emotions, desires, or impulses.\n\nWRITING:\n- {自|じ} (self)\n- {制|せい} (control, regulate)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {自制|じせい}する (to exercise self-control - suru verb)\n- {自制心|じせいしん} (self-control, willpower - noun)\n- {自制|じせい}を{失|うしな}う (to lose self-control)\n- {自制|じせい}が{効|き}く (to have self-control working)\n- More internal/psychological than {抑制|よくせい} (restraint)\n- Implies conscious effort and willpower\n- Can refer to controlling emotions, appetite, spending, etc.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {自制|じせい}を{保|たも}つ (to maintain self-control)\n- {自制|じせい}を{促|うなが}す (to urge self-restraint)\n- {自制|じせい}の{効|き}いた (self-controlled, composed)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {抑制|よくせい} (restraint, suppression)\n- {忍耐|にんたい} (patience, endurance)\n- {節制|せっせい} (moderation, temperance)\n- {我慢|がまん} (patience, self-control)",
